    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_01\" id=\"tag_17_521_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "setenv — add or change environment variable",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_02\" id=\"tag_17_521_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00004",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]\n[CODE4]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt><sup>[<a href=\"javascript:open_code('CX')\">CX</a>]</sup> <img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\"> #include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/stdlib.h.html\">stdlib.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint setenv(const char *</tt><i>envname</i><tt>, const char *</tt><i>envval</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>overwrite</i><tt>); <img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\"></tt></code>"
     },
     "CODE4": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt><br></tt>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A5][/A5]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A5": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_03\" id=\"tag_17_521_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I6]setenv[/I6]() function shall update or add a variable in the environment of the calling process. The [I7]envname[/I7]\nargument points to a string containing the name of an environment variable to be added or altered. The environment variable shall\nbe set to the value to which [I8]envval[/I8] points. The function shall fail if [I9]envname[/I9] points to a string which contains an\n[CODE10] character. If the environment variable named by [I11]envname[/I11] already exists and the value of [I12]overwrite[/I12] is\nnon-zero, the function shall return success and the environment shall be updated. If the environment variable named by\n[I13]envname[/I13] already exists and the value of [I14]overwrite[/I14] is zero, the function shall return success and the environment\nshall remain unchanged.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE10": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'='</tt>"
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I15]setenv[/I15]() function shall update the list of pointers to which [I16]environ[/I16] points.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The strings described by [I17]envname[/I17] and [I18]envval[/I18] are copied by this function.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The [I19]setenv[/I19]() function need not be thread-safe.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00010",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A20][/A20]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A20": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_04\" id=\"tag_17_521_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, zero shall be returned. Otherwise, -1 shall be returned, [I21]errno[/I21] set to indicate the error, and\nthe environment shall be unchanged.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I21": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00012",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A22][/A22]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A22": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_05\" id=\"tag_17_521_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00013",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I23]setenv[/I23]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00014",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00015",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I24]envname[/I24] argument points to an empty string or points to a string containing an [CODE25] character.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE25": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'='</tt>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00016",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[ENOMEM]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00017",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Insufficient memory was available to add a variable or its value to the environment.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00018",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A26][/A26]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A26": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_06\" id=\"tag_17_521_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00019",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00020",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A27][/A27]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A27": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_07\" id=\"tag_17_521_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "See [A28][I29]exec[/I29]()[/A28] for restrictions on changing the environment in multi-threaded\napplications.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A28": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/exec.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00022",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A30][/A30]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_521_08\" id=\"tag_17_521_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00023",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Unanticipated results may occur if [I31]setenv[/I31]() changes the external variable [I32]environ[/I32]. In particular, if the optional\n[I33]envp[/I33] argument to [I34]main[/I34]() is present, it is not changed, and thus may point to an obsolete copy of the environment (as\nmay any other copy of [I35]environ[/I35]). However, other than the aforementioned restriction, the standard developers intended that\nthe traditional method of walking through the environment by way of the [I36]environ[/I36] pointer must be supported.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00024",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "It was decided that [I37]setenv[/I37]() should be required by this version because it addresses a piece of missing functionality,\nand does not impose a significant burden on the implementor.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00025",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "There was considerable debate as to whether the System V [A38][I39]putenv[/I39]()[/A38] function or the\nBSD [I40]setenv[/I40]() function should be required as a mandatory function. The [I41]setenv[/I41]() function was chosen because it\npermitted the implementation of the [A42][I43]unsetenv[/I43]()[/A42] function to delete environmental\nvariables, without specifying an additional interface. The [A44][I45]putenv[/I45]()[/A44] function is\navailable as part of the XSI option.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A38": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A42": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/unsetenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I43": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A44": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I45": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00026",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The standard developers considered requiring that [I46]setenv[/I46]() indicate an error when a call to it would result in exceeding\n{ARG_MAX}. The requirement was rejected since the condition might be temporary, with the application eventually reducing the\nenvironment size. The ultimate success or failure depends on the size at the time of a call to [I47][A48]exec[/A48][/I47], which returns an indication of this error condition.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A48": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/exec.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00027",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     9
    ],
    "text": "See also the RATIONALE section in [A49][I50]getenv[/I50]()[/A49].",
    "placeholders": {
     "A49": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/getenv.html#\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I50": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
